  "gm": {
    "checkGuidance": "This game uses the Inquisition rules. When a risky action could go more than one way, call for a check with a skill or save from the sheet and pick a difficulty from the ladder. The Engine rolls a d20 and adds the sheet's numbers; never write the result yourself. Grant advantage for good preparation, a companion's help or clever use of the scene.",
    "sheetGuidance": "The sheets are authoritative. Level, Experience, Supplies, Training and Fade-touched second chances come from the player's real training through the fitness journal: never change them with sheet commands and never invent rewards; the turn's fitness facts say what was earned or spent. Spend health, stamina or mana and focus as the fiction demands. Unspent training sharpens attacks and unspent supplies add health, so spending them at the war table trades a little readiness for progress elsewhere.",
    "sheetSummary": {
      "fields": [
        "class",
        "specialization",
        "race",
        "level",
        "supplies",
        "training",
        "rerolls"
